<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 17 February, from 1600 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1600</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Giordano Bruno is burned at the stake in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Condemned by the Inquisition for heresy, the Dominican philosopher was burned in the Campo de' Fiori. His views included an infinite universe with countless worlds; a statue of him now stands there.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1801</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">House elects Thomas Jefferson President after an electoral tie</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the 36th ballot, the House of Representatives broke the tie between Jefferson and his running mate Aaron Burr. The crisis led to the Twelfth Amendment, separating votes for President and Vice-President.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1863</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Committee that became the Red Cross meets in Geneva</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Five Genevans, including Henri Dunant, founded a committee to aid wounded soldiers, inspired by Dunant's account of Solferino. It became the International Committee of the Red Cross.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1864</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">H. L. Hunley sinks USS Housatonic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Confederate submarine rammed a torpedo into the Union warship off Charleston, the first sinking of an enemy ship by a submarine. The Hunley was lost with all eight crew that night.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1933</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First issue of News-Week is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The weekly news magazine, later Newsweek, was launched in New York as a rival to Time. It became one of the leading American news weeklies of the 20th century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1979</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">China invades Vietnam</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Chinese troops crossed Vietnam's northern border to punish Hanoi for invading Cambodia. Both sides claimed victory after a month of fighting that cost tens of thousands of lives.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a></div></li></ol>
